s new company allowing Combs  to hit the ground running in its first  year the young label released Mack's  flavor in a year which proved to be a  huge success this was followed with  albums by b.i.g which also went on to  become multi-platinum in 2002 Combs was  named one of the 40 richest people on  the forty by Fortune magazine with the  current estimated net worth of over  three hundred million dollars Combs has  become something of an American icon and  against all odds one of the country's  most successful entrepreneurs  by trusting his entrepreneurial  instincts and by having a courage to  follow them Combs was able to go from  the streets of Harlem into becoming one  of the most successful entrepreneurs in  the entertainment industry to help you  explode your business here are three  action items and you can learn from Sean  Combs action item number one work hard  modern success will help ensure that  you're focusing on the right tasks but  you still have to do the work starting  and running a business is one of the  most challenging things you'll ever do  in your life so commit to giving it your  best don't give up when things don't go  your way  focus on helping your target audience  and giving them incredible value with  hard work and time you'll get there  never one to shun hard work Combs is  willing to do whatever it took to get  his business off the ground and keep it  there he was a workaholic even from his  early entrepreneurial days at Howard  University and always made his business  ventures his number one priority eager  to succeed at Uptown records combs often  sacrifice both his academics and the  social life in order to rise in the  ranks of the business world he  frequently shuddered back between New  York City and Washington DC trying to  balance both school and work  it was his dedication and hard work that  marked his rise to the top which is one  of the most rapid ascents in a history  of the music industry according that  Combs  I came in to win this is why I stay up  late while other people are sleeping  this is why I don't go out to the  Hamptons I've never been surprised about  what's happened to me I've put in hard  work to get to this point it's like when  you become a lawyer if you're busting  your ass you're not surprised when you  get your degree this is my plan when I'm  in the studio making a hit record I'm  not trying to make a hit record I'm  making one this is what I studied this  is why I stay up 20 hours a day I'm  trying to be somebody I didn't come into  this business saying I'm going to look  like the biggest black man in music I  was like I'm going to be the biggest I'm  going to go down in history as being one  of the best music men and business men  in entertainment  action the number to take risks if you  wait until you have all the information  you need to make a decision you'll be  too late you don't have to be a gambler  to be an entrepreneur but you have to be  willing to take calculated risks bet on  yourself and have the confidence to know  that you can succeed at whatever you do  if you put your mind to it  from the very first day Combs began his  internship at Uptown records he had it  in the back of his mind that one day he  would start his own company he wasn't  even thinking on the scale of Uptown  Combs wanted to be bigger as big as they  come and he knew that in order to get  there he couldn't do it alone with the  likes of Clive Davis and the notorious  b.i.g I decide come set out to achieve  his goals he did it by pushing a limits  what was expected to this end com said  out about revolutionising the music  industry by exploring new territory in a  fresh concept Combs had his 1997 hip hot  hit single it's all about the Benjamins  reworked by Rob Zombie and David Grohl  to create a hugely successful Rock remix  he also surprised many by sampling  musics from the likes of David Bowie in  the police mixing them with his light  rap rhythms combs was never afraid to 